WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.860
Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker has divided
fans in a big way, and perhaps we shouldn't

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:06.280
be too surprised about that.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:11.000
The final installment of the Skywalker saga
hit theaters on Thursday, December 19th…

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.940
and since then, responses to the film have
been pouring in across social media.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.360
So far, professional critics haven't been
particularly impressed by the movie - with

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:23.820
many reviewers arguing that the installment
provides too much fan service and too little

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:24.440
substance.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:28.960
Meanwhile, plenty of viewers have taken to
Twitter to both praise and scorn the film.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.500
Honestly, reactions have been all over the
map.

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:36.020
Make no mistake: Plenty of diehard Star Wars
fans stayed up late on Thursday night to catch

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:40.020
the premiere… and many of them had nothing
but good things to say about the film.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.060
One fan tweeted,

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:41.560
"I loved it.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.420
For me, it provided perfect closure.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:46.880
The acting, the effects, the action sequences...
all brilliant.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:51.120
I've loved Star Wars since the 80's and I
was not let down by #RiseofSkywalker To all

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.680
those involved, from past to present...

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:54.180
I thank you."

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:58.300
At least one longtime fan of the franchise
fully agreed with that assessment, writing,

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:02.820
"The Rise of Skywalker embodies everything
I love about Star Wars, and it never skips

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:03.340
a beat.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:05.540
A perfect ending to the Skywalker Saga.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:08.660
Take it from a kid born in 1977, it's epic."

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:13.240
Another fan praised the lead performances
and the direction in no uncertain terms, tweeting:

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.440
"J.J. Abrams did an incredible job.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:17.160
I felt every second of this movie!

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:20.020
The acting is the best I've seen in Star Wars
history.

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:22.200
[...] Daisy Ridley and Adam Driver killed
it!"

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:27.080
Given the controversial reception of The Last
Jedi in 2017, perhaps we shouldn't be too

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:31.409
shocked that some fans heaped praise on The
Rise of Skywalker while totally bashing its

00:01:31.409 --> 00:01:31.900
predecessor.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.000
One such fan tweeted:

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.160
"Forget the bad reviews this is a blast!

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:39.620
J.J. Abrams managed to fix the [Rian] Johnson
mess from the last movie and give a thrill

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:40.780
ride at the same time.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:41.960
The fans will love it.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:42.580
Great job!"

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:44.860
Adding fuel to the fire, another fan wrote
that

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:49.220
"[The Rise of Skywalker is] a great movie
and it's the best one out of the new trilogy.

00:01:49.229 --> 00:01:54.039
The Last Jedi was a disaster of a movie and
JJ Abrams did what he could to save the series."

00:01:54.039 --> 00:01:57.869
Meanwhile, countless fans of the franchise
were deeply disappointed by the film, and

00:01:57.869 --> 00:02:01.009
they certainly didn't hold back when it came
to voicing that displeasure.

00:02:01.009 --> 00:02:04.329
One detractor tweeted,
"After a 2nd viewing I can confidently say

00:02:04.329 --> 00:02:07.360
that Star Wars IX: Rise of Skywalker BLOWS.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:12.400
It's the perfect confluence of horrible pacing,
uncomfortable close ups, terribly inconsistent

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:16.140
use of their own [canon], and forced Star
Wars cliches ad nauseam."

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:18.740
Another viewer was similarly unimpressed,
tweeting,

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.800
"Rise of Skywalker was absolutely terrible.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:24.260
You could tell J.J. really tried, but it was
a mess.

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:26.260
A sequel to a movie we never saw."

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:29.270
On the other hand, one fan seemed totally
conflicted, tweeting:

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:32.920
"The Rise of Skywalker is the worst movie
I have ever loved.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.400
It was a dumpster fire of fanfiction tropes
that made no sense.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:39.940
There was no character development that made
sense, there were no stakes.

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:42.800
It was a trash movie.  But it was my trash."

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:47.349
Rest assured, plenty of big names shared their
reactions, too - and those reactions run the

00:02:47.349 --> 00:02:49.300
gamut from delight to disgust.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:53.180
Fanboys director Kyle Newman was clearly satisfied
with the film, writing:

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:57.020
"Advice to fellow #StarWars fans: Don't let
the critics get you down!!!

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:58.600
Go have a [...] blast at the theater.

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:01.240
There are so many great things about #TheRiseOfSkywalker.

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:02.880
It's flawed but it's FUN.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:05.880
And don't forget to bring that kid who lives
inside you as your guest.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:06.600
They'll dig it."

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.360
On the other hand, English writer, director,
and actor Jack Howard tweeted that

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:13.890
"[The Rise of Skywalker] ends the new trilogy
with a disappointing whimper.

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:18.519
It plays out like a fan film, back-peddling
decisions in The Last Jedi in favour of connecting

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:22.360
dots to satisfy a specific group rather than
tell an original story.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.900
It feels like the series is at war with itself."

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:29.040
ESPN writer Ryan McGee revealed his own thoughts
on the film, tweeting that,

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.780
"I haven't looked at the Tomatometer for #RiseofSkywalker
because I legitimately don't care.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:37.730
Took my daughter, like I have her whole life,
and we laughed and cried and went 'Whoa!'

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:38.840
and had a helluva time.

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:41.940
Just like I did with my family 30+ years ago.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:43.600
To me, that's the magic of it."

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:49.020
As we said, reactions are all over the place, and we don't expect the debates to die down anytime soon

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:53.760
. On the upside, at least The Rise of Skywalker
has made us all stop talking about the "Maclunkey!"

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:54.260
debacle.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:54.940
"Maclunkey!"

